WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.609
Day had broken, and the world as we knew it
fell to pieces.

00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:10.769
On every corner of the globe, devastating
rays of sunshine have liquified most of the

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:12.200
human race.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:17.770
The anomalous phenomenon known as SCP-001
had made the most treasured source of light

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:23.490
and life in the galaxy into the harbinger
of a planetary apocalypse.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:28.430
In the streets of major cities, which were
once so filled with culture and activity,

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:35.000
melting abominations slithered along the sidewalks
and pavement: a cruel parody of the crowds

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.670
and traffic that existed in the world before.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:43.111
The drought-ravaged wilderness teems with
countless globs of mutant flesh that were

00:00:43.111 --> 00:00:46.100
once proud members of the animal kingdom.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.900
Even the plants have wilted into an inert
state, overwhelmed by the sun's energy to

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.340
the point of being unable to photosynthesize
it.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:59.289
There are no planes in the sky anymore, as
no pilot flying on that day could escape the

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:00.840
view of daylight.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.790
The boundless ocean is adrift with boats and
cruise liners occupied by an aimless crew

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:11.369
of amalgamations which even the initial survivors
on the lower decks and within the rooms have

00:01:11.369 --> 00:01:14.189
long since been assimilated into.

00:01:14.189 --> 00:01:19.869
In the early months of SCP-001 - When Day
Breaks - The Foundation had been able to distribute

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:24.860
rudimentary information on how to shield oneself
from the pervasive rays.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:30.110
This included a basic but comprehensive how-to
guide on building protective clothing that

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.159
would keep out all daylight.

00:01:32.159 --> 00:01:37.820
Unfortunately, there is only so much benefit
these solutions can provide - as it has become

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:43.070
too late to save the vast majority of humanity
from their terrible melting fate.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:47.640
There are sadly limits on what the Foundation’s
foresight and knowledge could do to prevent

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:53.560
a worst-case scenario, and many containment
sites were lost within the first 24 hours

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.759
alone.

00:01:54.759 --> 00:01:59.820
This means that the veil of normalcy that
SCP Foundation had fought so hard to preserve

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:02.430
has effectively ceased to exist.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:08.450
Most, if not all, of the accumulated research,
the containment procedures for dangerous anomalies,

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:12.920
and the skilled personnel who were brave and
foolish to think they could keep the world

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:17.040
safe, have met with terrible fates in this
solar-scarred hellscape.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.660
If there was ever an era where the planet
and the universe were stable and under the

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:27.110
control of The Foundation and the 05 council,
that time has passed.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:32.380
This is not their world anymore, nor is it
a world that can be ruled by any people.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:37.160
Day has broken, and this is a world of monsters.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:43.310
Today, two of these monsters, in particular,
find themselves on a collision course.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:48.640
Both were once extremely dangerous Keter-class
SCPs contained by The Foundation, but through

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:54.260
circumstance and ingenuity, both anomalies
had freed themselves and adapted to the harsh

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:56.690
new reality of the outside world.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:04.170
They were known as SCP-076-2 Able and SCP-682,
respectively.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:08.840
Able - now known in the fireside stories of
human survivors as The Black Warrior - had

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:14.060
given himself an armored makeover by forging
his many weapons into a day-proof second skin

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.769
straight out of dark fantasy media.

00:03:16.769 --> 00:03:21.819
This new edgy gothic look came complete with
a massive sword that Able could use to cleave

00:03:21.819 --> 00:03:25.870
straight through any fleshy freakshow he encountered
in the wasteland.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:32.920
He was a true living legend now - a mysterious
hero, a violent demon, and a force of nature

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:33.980
all at once.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:38.490
In the day, he stalked through the ruins of
civilization, finding whatever passed for

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.590
worthy opponents and cutting them down.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:44.980
At night, he would seek out those depraved
souls who would prey upon their fellow human

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:47.330
and put them to the sword.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:51.849
These malefactors had recently become Able’s
favorite vermin to exterminate, since they

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:56.390
always seemed so surprised to be on the receiving
end of an ambush.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:00.180
Being a survivor in this hellish new world
was difficult enough without the additional

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:05.239
strain of plotting violence, so the ones who
took advantage of the absence of laws and

00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:10.629
did so were either exceedingly clever or simply
driven out of their wits by the desire to

00:04:10.629 --> 00:04:11.890
inflict harm.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:16.790
It was through several experiences stomping
out the lingering scum of the Earth that Able

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:20.209
discovered an unfamiliar sense of honor within
himself.

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:25.880
It wasn’t that he grew accustomed to protecting
frail humans from monsters, but rather the

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:31.660
simple fact that a good fight required two
mutually adversarial parties.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:36.220
Bandits and serial killers could routinely
be counted on to have delusions of grandeur

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:40.690
accompanied by ill intentions, while their
hapless victims could not.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:45.440
In his own twisted way, Able had accepted
that showing mercy to cowards and weaklings

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.300
suited his ends.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:52.100
After all, if there were no more innocents
left alive there would also be no more reprobates

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.660
to menace them.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:59.090
His quarry needed something to bait them into
emerging from the shadows after all.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:03.660
Despite having made the most of slim picking,
there was a deep-seated part of Able that

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:05.560
longed for a real challenge.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.680
The Black Warrior wished to face a real monster
like himself again, not the petty brutes and

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.970
former human sludge he’d been using as substitutes.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:18.919
SCP-682 would be an ideal opponent, but he
hadn’t seen the reptile since he was back

00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:20.160
in containment.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.341
The two had been made to fight each other
the day before all of this began, and when

00:05:24.341 --> 00:05:30.030
during the containment breach that later ensued:
SCP-682 had a makeover of its own.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:35.130
The highly morphic lizard had tunneled its
way out of Site 19 by evolving large scooping

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:38.140
claws suited for subterranean travel.

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:43.600
Being surprisingly intelligent for its animalistic
shape, 682 had managed to torture the details

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:47.850
of the SCP-001 scenario out of an unlucky
researcher.

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:54.250
While Able had found a way to remain active
during both day and night, SCP-682 had become

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:57.090
a bit more selective in its schedule.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:01.460
This was possible because the creature had
adapted an internal clock by absorbing the

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:03.810
previously mentioned researcher’s wristwatch.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:09.520
When the sun was visible in the sky, 682 would
remain dormant underground.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:13.850
There it could bask in the symphony of suffering
from all the surface-dwelling living things

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.449
it could perceive with its enhanced hearing.

00:06:16.449 --> 00:06:21.380
It would lie in wait for hours, anticipating
the darkness of nightfall.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:28.770
Once the sun had set, SCP-682 would emerge
and devour both human and abomination alike.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:33.400
As a being that harbored pure hatred for all
things that lived, the reptile had far less

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.750
discerning criteria for acceptable targets
than Able.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:41.250
It unleashed its wrath on anything that so
much as got in its way during the nightly

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:42.740
feeding frenzy.

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:47.819
Another way that 682 differed from Able in
its post-apocalyptic way of life was that

00:06:47.819 --> 00:06:51.390
it hadn’t been given any evocative nickname
or title.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:57.110
The reason why was surprisingly simple: SCP-682
hadn’t made its existence known because

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:00.919
any survivors that encountered it never lived
to tell the tale.

00:07:00.919 --> 00:07:06.129
It was a surprise to both of them when late
one night, a twist of fate brought the monsters

00:07:06.129 --> 00:07:07.840
back together.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:13.590
SCP-682 had just resurfaced near a small encampment
of survivors and was approaching with the

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:16.720
intention to massacre the panicking humans.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.680
As the hateful reptile drew closer, it noticed
a dark figure lurking at the other side of

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:22.680
the campfire.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:27.720
It was roughly the size of an average humanoid,
but instead of running and screaming, the

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:31.300
figure stood firm with an enormous sword in
one hand.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:34.389
One of the fleeing humans cried out, “It’s
the Black Warrior!

00:07:34.389 --> 00:07:35.770
We’re saved!”

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:42.110
This amused 682, and it sported a sadistic
grin as it ran towards the survivor and pounced.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:46.289
While the lizard had wanted to demonstrate
how flimsy the human’s sense of salvation

00:07:46.289 --> 00:07:49.539
really was, the opposite took place.

00:07:49.539 --> 00:07:54.409
The so-called Black Warrior had intercepted
its jaws and was blocking 682 with only his

00:07:54.409 --> 00:07:58.020
sword and all the superhuman strength he could
put behind it.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:01.340
“Go now, little ant,” The Black Warrior
said.

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:06.380
Following Able’s command, the human fled,
looking back over its shoulder only once to

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:09.500
gaze at the Black Warrior in silent awe.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:13.941
With that straggler gone, the two monsters
were now completely alone in the camp, both

00:08:13.941 --> 00:08:16.830
illuminated by the orange glow of firelight.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:20.150
They separated and began to circle each other.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:25.030
Memories of their old rivalry began flooding
back as both of the now-liberated keter-classes

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.970
confirmed the identity of the other.

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:33.279
SCP-682 began to laugh as it recognized the
stance of the ancient warrior that had been

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:35.899
such a thorn in its side back in containment.

00:08:35.899 --> 00:08:36.899
“Isn’t this priceless?

00:08:36.899 --> 00:08:46.270
The proud and merciless Able has become a
defender of those disgusting humans,” SCP-682

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:49.490
said, wearing that horrible smile once again.

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:53.269
“I’m not fighting for them,” The Black
Warrior answered.

00:08:53.269 --> 00:08:57.580
He lunged forward, striking a hard blow against
682’s carapace.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:09:01.860
The edged sword bounced upward in recoil,
but not without inflicting a deep wound that

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:05.610
682’s regeneration began to work overtime
to repair.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:10.030
The reptile swiped at Able with its scoop-claws,
then made further use of them by burrowing

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:12.140
into the ground below.

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:16.029
Able knew better than to follow the creature
underground, and he was almost sure that his

00:09:16.029 --> 00:09:18.269
scaly nemesis hadn’t yet retreated.

00:09:18.269 --> 00:09:23.850
He held his ground and waited, steeling himself
for the moment the creature revealed itself

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:25.200
once more.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:28.620
As expected, the attack came from directly
below.

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:33.940
SCP-682 breached the surface and snapped its
jaws around one of Able’s armored legs.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:38.080
Trusting his instincts, the Black Warrior
struck back in the same moment.

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:42.519
His sword stabbed into the reptile’s jaws,
and with a bit of strength, he leveraged his

00:09:42.519 --> 00:09:44.150
own leg free.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:50.620
The armor was dented, but fortunately, there
were no apparent holes left by 682’s fangs.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:55.610
Able had become accustomed to diligently maintaining
the condition of his armor, as even the smallest

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:59.970
crack could - in the daylight hours - cause
him to lose his solid form forever.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:05.470
He’d make sure to do a more thorough investigation
later, after the lizard had been put in its

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:06.470
place.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:11.300
The Black Warrior fought defensively, minimizing
the damage to his armor while timing his strikes

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:15.370
to keep 682 from overwhelming him with sheer
offense.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:19.860
He could certainly go all out if he chose
to, but that same part of him that wanted

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:24.810
a challenge was willing to prolong the conflict
- especially if he could save himself the

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.540
trouble of repairs later.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:32.600
SCP-682, on the other hand, didn’t care
much for being taken lightly, and was astute

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:36.340
enough to notice when his foe wasn’t as
aggressive as usual.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:40.700
It had been over a year since the monsters
had fought, but this time there would be no

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.870
Foundation personnel to end the fight prematurely.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:50.529
682 decided that it was time to give the armored
edgelord an onslaught that he couldn’t ignore.

00:10:50.529 --> 00:10:55.690
It began to rotate its tunneling claws like
a pair of pneumatic excavators and instantly

00:10:55.690 --> 00:11:00.970
showered The Black Warrior with dirt and debris
as it burrowed back into the Earth.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:05.741
Able could deflect the rocks easily enough,
but the temporary distraction gave 682 time

00:11:05.741 --> 00:11:10.570
to dig a large enough cavern beneath Able’s
feet that the ground instantly collapsed beneath

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.120
his armored bulk.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:18.170
Able slid into the growing pit and straight
towards the twin grinding claws of 682.

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:22.100
He tried to use his sword in the ground to
slow his descent, but the earth had been so

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:26.990
thoroughly tenderized by his opponent that
all he accomplished was hastening it.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:33.010
Just like an antlion larva, SCP-682 had created
a death pit of detritus that was pulling Able

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.110
towards the center of the trap.

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:40.300
As if making a whirlpool on land wasn’t
crazy enough for 682, the reptile grew itself

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:44.140
an array of impaling horns across the front
of its face and snout.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:48.779
Though constructed of flesh and bone, they
had the appearance of serrated blades and

00:11:48.779 --> 00:11:53.041
possessed a sharpness and durability capable
of penetrating through Able’s fancy new

00:11:53.041 --> 00:11:54.860
suit of armor.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:59.260
But the Black Warrior wasn’t going to be
defeated so easily, especially not after all

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:03.730
the work he had put in during his latest life
to forge these armaments.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:07.980
While clutching his giant blade in one hand,
he conjured a new weapon from the shadows:

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:13.970
a harpoon with a strong chain that appeared
already wrapped tightly around his black gauntlet.

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:17.820
Able hurled the harpoon behind him with as
much strength as he could manage in his nearly

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:22.910
prone state, and as he had hoped, its tip
embedded itself in the more stable ground

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.980
past the edge of the death pit.

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:29.470
With the spear firmly secured at the other
end, the chain went taught and Able was able

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:34.880
to stop himself just short of falling on SCP-682’s
facial spikes.

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:39.360
With a tremendous one-handed swing that would
be impossible for a mortal man, Able cut through

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:44.300
the middle of the lizard’s organic bayonets,
rendering them practically useless.

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:49.100
His metal boots dug into the silt, and with
all his strength he wrenched himself backwards

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:53.459
towards the top of the pit, tearing the harpoon
free in the process.

00:12:53.459 --> 00:12:57.330
With acute precision, he used the chain to
direct the tip of the harpoon between the

00:12:57.330 --> 00:13:01.420
fractured bone-blades and into 682’s skull.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:05.730
The creature bellowed from the sudden pain
and began to dig downward again, but by this

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:11.060
time Able was on stable earth again and was
pulling with all his strength on the other

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.920
side of the chain.

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:18.220
SCP-682 burrowed as furiously as it could,
but the harpoon embedded in its head was throwing

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:20.130
off its equilibrium.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:25.019
Able planted his feet and kept pulling, summoning
more weapons around his feet and legs to keep

00:13:25.019 --> 00:13:27.740
them from moving an inch back towards the
pit.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:32.671
It was a titan’s tug of war, and whoever
gave in would surely be at the mercy of the

00:13:32.671 --> 00:13:33.671
other.

00:13:33.671 --> 00:13:38.639
Neither monster wavered and the thing that
broke under the strain was the chain itself.

00:13:38.639 --> 00:13:43.840
682 tunneled away – harpoon still scratching
its brain – and did not surface again that

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:48.570
night, while The Black Warrior staggered as
he retrieved his now broken length of the

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:49.570
chain.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:53.850
Able waited for his hated foe to resurface,
but the creature had apparently decided it

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:56.500
was no longer interested in a fight.

00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:01.529
And it was just as well, because in the east,
the sun was rising again.

00:14:01.529 --> 00:14:05.449
The Black Warrior moved inside one of the
tents that the survivors had left behind,

00:14:05.449 --> 00:14:08.390
and prepared for a full examination of his
armor.

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:15.029
While it didn’t last, and no SCP save for
SCP-001 could claim victory here, Able was

00:14:15.029 --> 00:14:20.500
grateful to know their still proper adversaries
to fight after the end.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.940
Want to own an SCP of your own?

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:25.760
Go to scpswag.com for premium anomalous merchandise!

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:32.230
Now go check out “Could SCP-076 - Able Survive
SCP-001 - When Day Breaks?”

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:37.839
and “SCP-001 When Day Breaks SCP-682”
to see how it all started!

